# What GitHub's language bar is allowed to count.
#
# The repository is a single Rust crate carrying a large committed evidence
# tree. `reference/` alone (the upstream fork, the spike notes, the workflow
# archive) outweighs `src/` in bytes, and its shell and Python make the bar
# report a majority-Shell project — a claim about the repo that is false in
# every sense a reader means it. linguist-vendored says "committed, but not
# ours": the files stay tracked and diffable, and stop being counted.
#
# `reference-corpus/` and `.sergeant/` are marked ahead of their arrival: they
# exist on the N-series branch today, and marking them here means the language
# bar survives that merge unchanged rather than needing a follow-up.
reference/** linguist-vendored
reference-corpus/** linguist-vendored
.sergeant/** linguist-vendored

# Machine-written, reviewed only as a lockfile.
Cargo.lock linguist-generated
